# Revisions to skip when running `git blame`.
#
# Mass reformats bury authorship: without this file, `git blame` on any of the
# 86 swept files attributes every line to the formatting commit rather than to
# whoever wrote the code.
#
# Use it with:
#     git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs <file>
#
# Or once, per clone, to make it automatic:
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# One full-length SHA per line, newest last, with a comment naming the change.
# A SHA can only be added *after* the commit exists, so a reformat lands first
# and its SHA is appended in the commit that follows.

